{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4566","id":4735363994,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU59Ms88AAAABGj_rmg","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4566","diff_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4566.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4566.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/issues/4566","number":4566,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"A00: keep compiler diagnostic callers on registered IDs","user":{"login":"wieslawsoltes","id":2297442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTc0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2297442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Why\n\nThe Project 4 full-CI run [37210639599](https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/actions/runs/37210639599/job/111460940659) found compiler callers that reintroduced raw diagnostic strings after the catalog migration. Fixing its first reported file exposed one more caller in speculative semantic binding.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Use already imported `DiagnosticId.CS1593` and `DiagnosticId.CS7036` for delegate argument-count comparisons in `binder/body/calls.js`.\n- Import the existing mapping and use `DiagnosticId.CS0103` for the missing-binder result in `semantic/model-scopes.js`.\n\nThese constants equal the original strings. Diagnostic codes, messages, arguments, spans and branch behavior are preserved. No catalog entries, IDs, contract tests or test expectations change.\n\nThe raw comparisons arrived through #3522 and the speculative-binding emission through #3551 after parallel catalog work. The complete lexical review used the existing test predicate across 566 compiler JavaScript files: two catalog exemptions and 564 callers.\n\n## Validation and history\n\nThe final committed source `7132306bc9d86b691cd11529c1c7a48900dee075`, tree `0547f7787aff8f12bc9cb9081bb5db6d0277557e`, passed **31/31 tests**, with no failures, skips or cancellations, through the serial limiter:\n\n- `tests/a00-diagnostic-ids.test.js`\n- `tests/compiler-diagnostic-spans.test.js`\n- `tests/compiler-semantic-model-analysis.test.js`\n- `tests/compiler-semantic-model.test.js`\n\nThe earlier one-file correction's 9-pass/1-fail result is retained: its behavioral tests passed, and the source scan exposed the additional CS0103 omission. Both focused commits are preserved; only the final tree is represented as passing. Final published head `cf0d5621cabca85fddc5ba6b56761e472ac153a9` has the same verified tree as the tested local head.\n\n## Scope and remaining qualification\n\nAll 98 claim refs and 13 lock refs were checked, including preserved legacy path scopes and a fresh ref comparison. Neither caller file has an advertised path reservation. The separately owned SF-A00-T14 catalog task, tests, claim, and status are preserved; this narrow caller repair does not transfer ownership.\n\nThe original full-CI run remains failed. The value-inventory correction landed in #4565, while the separate root-provider documentation/test correction remains reserved. This PR does not claim full qualification or close an issue.\n\nTask reference: SF-A00-T14